lesson: 239
title: Toys, rows and groups
level: primary-3
stars: 2
explain: Things set out in equal rows are counted by multiplying: rows × how many in each row.
explain: If some of the places are empty, broken or missing, take them away from the full count.
explain: A bus has 12 rows of 4 seats and 5 seats are empty: 12 × 4 = 48 seats, 48 − 5 = 43 people sitting.
vars: a=name r=3..12 k=3..6 e=2..9 d=2..9
need: r * k >= 2 * e + 6
answer: r * k - e
exercise: A bus has {r} rows of {k} seats. {e} seats are empty. How many passengers are sitting down?
exercise: {a} plants seeds in {r} rows of {k}. {e} seeds do not come up. How many seedlings come up?
exercise: A house has {r} windows with {k} panes each, and {e} panes are broken. How many panes are not broken?
exercise: {a} builds {r} towers of {k} bricks each, then {e} bricks fall off. How many bricks are still on the towers?
exercise: In the hall there are {r} rows of {k} chairs. {e} chairs are empty. How many people are sitting?
exercise: {a} sets out {r} rows of {k} cupcakes and {e} get eaten. How many cupcakes are left?
exercise: bus got {r} rows of {k} seats, {e} empty. how many ppl sitting
exercise: planted {r} rows of {k+1}, no sorry {k} seeds, then {e} didnt grow. how many grew
exercise: {r} towers, {k} bricks each, then my lil bro knocked {e} off lol. how many bricks still up
exercise: hall's got {r} rows of {k} chairs, {e} empty, oh and teacher's standing. how many sitting
exercise: my mate says {r*k+e} kids sitting cos you add the empty ones?? {r} rows of {k}, {e} empty. how many sitting really
test: Every seat is taken except {e} on a bus with {k} seats in each of its {r} rows. How many people are seated?
test: {e} of the panes are cracked in {r} windows of {k} panes. How many panes are whole?
test: {k} seats a row, {r} rows, {e} free. how many taken
test: A small cinema has {r} rows with {k} seats each, and {e} of the seats are still free. How many seats are taken?
test: {e} seeds no show, {r} rows of {k} planted. how many came up
test: {a} has {r} trays with {k} muffins on each and gives away {e}. How many muffins does {a.he} have left?
test: A bus with {r} rows of {k} seats has {e} empty seats; {d} more people wait at the next stop. How many people are seated now?
exam: Determine the number of occupied seats on a vehicle comprising {r.words} rows of {k.words} seats, whereas {e} seats remain vacant.
exam: It is given that {r} rows of {k} seeds each were sown, of which {e} failed to germinate. Ascertain the number of seeds which germinated.
exam: Compute the quantity of intact window panes, given {r} windows of {k} panes each, of which {e} are broken.
exam: State the number of persons seated in an auditorium arranged in {r} rows of {k} chairs, it being given that {e} chairs are unoccupied.
exercise: A coach has {r} rows of {k} seats. {e} seats are empty because those passengers were under the weather and stayed at home. How many people are sitting down?
exercise: {r} rows of {k} chairs at the school play and {e} of them empty cos half the year's got the runs, gross. how many kids actually sitting there?
test: {a} planted {r} rows of {k} seedlings, but sadly {e} of them did not make it. How many seedlings survived?
